Hi,
If you have access to JAWS, you can use the JAWS script called BX from
http://dlee.org
and Jamal's text editor for programmers called EdSharp.
I'm totally blind, and using a combination of these, and the system =
calculator for calculating percentages, is how I built WhatSock.com and =
all of the user interface component downloads.=20
I'd be happy to show you the trick of it if you like, just let me know.

=20
  ----- Original Message -----=20
  From: Andy B.=20
  To: program-l@freelists.org=20
  Sent: Saturday, April 28, 2012 1:32 PM
  Subject: [program-l] Web development in linux


  I use orca in Ubuntu 12.04. I need to find a reliable way to do web =
development. This means that I need to make sure that styles and css =
code turn out the way it needs to. Since orca is displaying pages in the =
way a sighted person would use it, it makes it difficult to do anything =
with. Does anyone have any ideas? Is firebug going to be the way I need =
to go on this?

  =20

